From eb7a6a544fe8867e8ff458acef8f45e6ad09106f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:38:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Noah-MP: move truncated thin snow to the soil instead of
 deleting it

Noah-MP sets snow without layers to zero when snowh <= 1e-6 m or
sneqv <= 1e-3 mm (energy, snowh2o, and the end of noahmp_sflx), and the water
goes nowhere. Ice dripping off the canopy (precip_heat) reaches the ground as
~1e-4 mm of snowfall per step, so on snow-free ground snowh2o deleted it
every step.

Add the truncated snow to the top soil layer as ice, as snowh2o already does
with excess sublimation. Snow with layers is unchanged. The glacier module (noahmp_glacier) has its
own thin-snow truncations, which this commit does not change.

Port of ufs-community/ccpp-physics fix H (same code), measured in UFS
(C96 control_p8_ugwpv1, 24 h, 1.77M soil column-steps): errwat summed to
-15.6 mm, all of it in this truncation (-0.009 % of global precipitation);
with the fix -0.014 mm, the remainder being fix I.

Measured with the rest of this series in the land component
(datm_cdeps_lnd_gswp3, 24 h, a water meter in noahmpdrv_run): Noah-MP's
water-check residual summed over land points was -1.50 mm (-5.2e-4 of the
precipitation, one-signed) before the series and -2.3e-9 mm (-8e-13) after;
the metered original reproduces the regression baseline.

AI-assisted: written with Claude Code (Anthropic); reviewed by the author.
---
 src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90 | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90 b/src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
index d7e8d97..b918b95 100644
--- a/src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
+++ b/src/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
@@ -943,6 +943,8 @@ contains
     end if
 
     if(snowh <= 1.e-6 .or. sneqv <= 1.e-3) then
+     ! the truncated snow goes to the top soil layer as ice
+     if(isnow == 0) smc(1) = smc(1) + sneqv/(dzsnso(1)*1000.)
      snowh = 0.0
      sneqv = 0.0
     end if
@@ -2045,6 +2047,8 @@ endif   ! croptype == 0
 
      fsno = 0.
      if(snowh <= 1.e-6 .or. sneqv <= 1.e-3) then
+       ! the truncated snow goes to the top soil layer as ice
+       if(isnow == 0) smc(1) = smc(1) + sneqv/(dzsnso(1)*1000.)
        snowh = 0.0
        sneqv = 0.0
      end if
@@ -8160,6 +8164,8 @@ zolmax = xkrefsqr / sqrt(xkzo)   ! maximum z/L
    end if
 
    if(snowh <= 1.e-6 .or. sneqv <= 1.e-3) then
+     ! the truncated snow goes to the top soil layer as ice
+     if(isnow == 0) sice(1) = sice(1) + sneqv/(dzsnso(1)*1000.)
      snowh = 0.0
      sneqv = 0.0
    end if
